(vox-elf: write a static x86-64 executable from a raw image and the
 manifest that says where its sections go, or lay the sections out first
 so the image can be assembled for the right addresses. The work is the
 voxelf library's; this program reads the command line, makes one call,
 and passes the diagnostics on to standard error.)

see "./voxelf.vox".

A flag called 'wants help' is "--help" or "-h", it is a boolean.
A flag called 'output path' is "--output" or "-o", it is a text.
A flag called 'entry name' is "--entry" or "-e", it is a text with default "_start".
A flag called 'wants a layout' is "--layout" or "-l", it is a boolean.
Parse flags.

A text called program is arguments's name.

If 'wants help' then,
    Print "Usage: {program} [OPTION]... MANIFEST -o OUTPUT",
    Print "Write the static x86-64 executable that MANIFEST describes to OUTPUT.",
    Print "MANIFEST names an image of raw section bytes, as nasm -f bin writes one,",
    Print "and says where each section lies in it and what it holds.",
    Print "\nOptions:",
    Print "  -o, --output FILE  write to FILE; there is no default",
    Print "  -e, --entry NAME   start the program at the symbol NAME (default _start)",
    Print "  -l, --layout       place the sections MANIFEST lists and write the",
    Print "                     placed manifest to FILE instead of an executable",
    Print "  -h, --help         display this help and exit",
    Print "\nThe executable is written with mode 0644, so make it executable with chmod.",
    Print "The exit status is the number of errors, or 255 when there are more than",
    Print "255, and each error is one line on standard error.",
    Exit 0.

Open a file for writing called 'error stream' at 2 (standard error).

a list called 'manifest paths' is arguments's all.
If 'manifest paths''s length is not 1 then,
    Write "{program}: name exactly one manifest; try --help\n" to 'error stream',
    Exit 2.
If 'output path' is empty then,
    Write "{program}: name the output with -o; try --help\n" to 'error stream',
    Exit 2.

a text called 'manifest path' is element 1 of 'manifest paths'.
Create a buffer called diagnostics.
a number called 'error count' is 0.
If 'wants a layout' then,
    Set 'error count' to 'lay out and count the errors' with 'manifest path' and 'output path' and diagnostics.
Otherwise,
    Set 'error count' to 'link and count the errors' with 'manifest path' and 'output path' and 'entry name' and diagnostics.
Write diagnostics to 'error stream'.
(An exit status is one byte, so a count it cannot hold is reported as its
 largest value, as the help says)
If 'error count' is greater than 255 then, Set 'error count' to 255.
Exit 'error count'.
